  "text_md": "## Food Act 2001-14.12.2017\n\n## 14~Sale of unsafe food\n\n- 1) A person must not sell food that the person knows is unsafe.\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- a If the offender is a body corporate\n- b) If the offender is a natural person imprisonment for four years.\n- person must not sell food that the person ought reasonably to know is unsafe.\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- a If the offender is a body corporate 8375 000.\n- (b) If the offender is a natural person 875 000.\n\n## 15~False description of food\n\n- 1) A person must not cause food intended for sale to be falsely described if the person knows that a consumer of the food who relies on the description will, or is likely suffer physical harm. to,\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- a If the offender is a body corporate S500 000.\n- b) If the offender is a natural person S100 000 or imprisonment for four years.\n- person must not cause food intended for sale to be falsely described if the person ought reasonably to know that a consumer of the food who relies on the description is likely to suffer physical harm:\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- (a) If the offender is a body corporate S375 000.\n- b) If the offender is a natural person S75 000.\n- (3) person must not sell food that the person knows\n- a) is falsely described; and\n- b) will cause, or is likely to cause, physical harm to a consumer of the food who relies on the description.\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- a) If the offender is a body corporate\n- b) If the offender is a natural person S100 000 or imprisonment for four years.\n3. A person must not sell food that the person ought reasonably to know\n- a) is falsely described; and\n5. (b) is likely to cause physical harm to a consumer of the food who relies on the description.\n\nMaximum penalty:\n\n- a If the offender is a body corporate 8375 000.\n- b If the offender is a natural person\n\nExamples of food that is falsely described are contained in section 22.\n\nNote",
